  "epic": "B3 #39",
  "command": "cargo run --release --locked -p weave-service --example load -- --clients 50 --seconds 20 --write-percent 20 --tenants 1 --auth api (one run per scenario; see each entry)",
  "source": "branch b3-service-load on top of B3 part 2 (PR #72, 52a9a8e) plus the load example; weave-engine store 32, protocol 1.1.0",
  "host": {
    "cpu": "AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 16 cores / 32 logical CPUs",
    "memory": "125 GiB",
    "os": "Linux 7.2.6 x86_64",
    "rustc": "rustc 1.98.1 (48a229cea 2026-09-01)",
    "storage": "local NVMe SSD, SQLite WAL, synchronous=FULL (defaults) for engine and audit stores",
    "note": "server and all clients on the same host over loopback; client TLS work shares the CPUs"
  },
  "workload": {
    "transport": "HTTP/1.1 over TLS 1.3 (rustls + ring), one keep-alive connection per client",
    "auth_path": "every request: bearer token lookup (API token digest or OIDC JWT signature + binding), registry standing check, engine call, audit append (fsync) before the response",
    "read": "POST /v1/execute: query of one seed node's outgoing weave:next edges, with fact_provenance",
    "write": "POST /v1/execute: one fact write asserting a node and an edge with service-minted IDs",
    "graph": "1,000 seed nodes and 1,000 edges per tenant, plus one settling write; writes add to it during the run",
    "warmup_seconds": 2,
    "latency": "client-observed, send to full response"
  },
  "findings": [
    "With one tenant, throughput is about 710 requests/s whatever the number of clients (1 client: 709/s; 50 clients: 709/s): the tenant runs one request at a time, so 50 clients queue and p50 latency rises to ~70 ms (p99 ~89 ms).",
    "OIDC costs the same as API tokens here (712.6 vs 708.7 requests/s).",
    "Across tenants, throughput scales to 2,318 requests/s at 5 tenants and 2,029 at 10, then falls (1,367 at 25, 1,103 at 50); the cause past 10 tenants was not established on this host (not fsync: synchronous=NORMAL on the audit log gave 1,177/s at 50 tenants).",
    "The audit fsync is a large share of single-tenant service time: an exploratory build with the audit log at synchronous=NORMAL gave 1,152 requests/s for one tenant and 50 clients, against 709 with the shipped synchronous=FULL. The shipped setting keeps FULL (see DECISIONS.md).",
    "A read at the head revision of a single bulk write (2,000 facts) took about 5 ms in the engine, against 0.45 ms after any further small write; the harness settles each graph with one small write. Reported to the engine owners as an A2 fact-store observation.",
    "No request failed in any scenario, and every tenant's audit hash chain verified after the run (audit_entries_verified)."
  ],
